# Weblication PHP-Framework (w* statt native PHP)

Gilt für **Projektcode** unter `rules*`. **`weblication/grid5/` nicht bearbeiten** (interner Kern).

In **Seiten-XML** (`rules/index.php` etc.): nach `<?php exit; ?>` nur XML/`wd:*` — keine PHP-Business-Logik einfügen; Logik in `pre.php`, Events oder XSLT-Templates.

## Substitutionen

| Statt | Nutze |
|-------|--------|
| `$_GET` / `$_POST` | `wRequest::getParameter()`, `getParameterInt()`, `getParameterText()` |
| XSS-kritisch | `getParameterSecure()` / `getParameterSecureStrict()` |
| State-changing Actions | `wRequest::checkActionToken()` / `checkFormToken()` |
| `file_get_contents` / `fopen` | `wReadWrite::readFile()` / `writeFile()` |
| CMS Datei/Verzeichnis | `wRepository::*` |
| `header('Location:…')` | `wResponse::redirect()` |
| `mail()` | `wMailer::sendMailStr()` / `sendMailHtml()` |
| XML escapen | `wStringconverter::convertToXml()` |
| `date()` Ausgabe | `wDate::formatDate()` / `displayFromTo()` |
| Pfade | `wPathName::createPathSecure()`, `getDirFile()`, … |
| XML/XPath | `wDOM::parseFile()`, `getValueOf()` |
| Dokumentdaten | `wDocumentData::getData()`, `getDataAsHTML()`, `setData()` |
| Listen / Navigation | `wList::createList()`, `wNavigation::createNavigationHTML()` |
| Cache | `wCache::clearCachePath()`, `clearCacheProject()` |
| Texte / Config | `wTexts::getText()`, `wVariables::getValue()` |
| Responsive Bilder | `wPicture::createPicture()` (statt festem `<img>`) |
| HTTP extern | `wNet::getUrlContent()` |
| Auth | `wUserCur::isLoggedIn()`, `isInGroup()` |

## Event-Beispiel (`onAfterSaveFile.wEvent.php`)

```php
$wSearch = new wSearch($eventData['projectPath'].'/weblication/project/searchs/default.wSearchBot.php');
$wSearch->addUrlToIndex($eventData['filePath'], true);
wCache::clearCacheProject($eventData['projectPath']);
```

